   "area_id": "ca_mount_starr_king_climbs",
   "name": "East Face",
   "grade": "5.7",
   "discipline": "trad",
   "overview": "Shortest approach: Mono Meadows trailhead, east about 8 km to the dome's foot, then south, scrambling a gully between two lower domes or circling round. Base: a tree beside an obvious dihedral; start low-left of it. P1 (5.6): easy flakes via the tree. P2 (5.7, crux): left to a crack, then a dihedral whose crack is shallow and flares open, lieback it; two-bolt anchor. P3 (5.7): left-slanting corner toward a small roof, wandering. P4: low 5th, final dihedral. Descent: three abseils on a 70 m rope, starting from a rocky outcrop on the south side.",
